<div class="page">
  <div class="section">
    <p>Please Note: The URTA candidate who receives a callback for the MFA Acting Program at Brooklyn College, and is interested in being considered for acceptance into our Program, must be submitted an application to the Graduate Admissions Office with a $75 application fee (required by Brooklyn College) prior to our in-house Brooklyn College auditions on the dates listed above. This permits both candidate and faculty an opportunity to learn more about each other and the program, after the brief experience URTA offers.</p>

    <h3>APPLICATION MATERIALS: What else to submit besides an application form?</h3>
    <p>In addition to completing Brooklyn College's online application for Graduate Admissions, all applicants must submit the following materials via the same online portal:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>A headshot and a resume.</li>
      <li>Three letters of recommendation.</li>
      <li>Official transcripts.</li>
      <li>An application fee of <span data-field="application_fee_amount">{{ application_fee_amount }}</span>.</li>
      <li>A three-page <span data-field="statement_of_intent">{{ statement_of_intent }}</span> explaining why the applicant wants to be considered for an MFA in Acting at Brooklyn College, and information about their artistic journey up to this point.</li>
      <li>A description of the applicant's current <span data-field="acting_preparation_process">{{ acting_preparation_process }}</span>: How do you approach the text and the development of a character before entering rehearsals for a play/scene? ("If it is not possible to submit two separate documents digitally, please put both the above essays into one document (items 4 and 5).")</li>
    </ol>
    <h4>AUDITION GUIDELINES:</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>The audition consists of two contrasting monologues: one classical (Shakespeare, Greek, Chekhov, Ibsen) and one contemporary.</li>
      <li>One monologue must be close to type. If you would like to include another skill that reveals your process as a developing artist, please bring that along.</li>
      <li>You will have three-four minutes for your audition in total. Your selections must reveal who you are and how you see yourself at this moment in your process.</li>
      <li>Applicants must audition in person unless that is not possible; only then will a Zoom audition or a self-tape submission be arranged.</li>
      <li>Bring a copy of a headshot and resume to the audition.</li>
      <li>Callbacks will take the form of a large group event. Should you receive a callback, please wear comfortable clothes in which you move easily.</li>
      <li>International candidates must be fluent in spoken and written English (A TOEFL score is required); and must contact the International Student Office for further information/requirements regarding the application process for international students.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>**Please note/recommendation process:</strong> The selection and admission process are based on the candidate's undergraduate and/or graduate and/or professional experience, written statements, and letters of recommendation.</p>
